      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1934 San Acacia Diversion Dam, built for irrigation, now sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/san_acacia_new_mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2006, the Rio Salado burst its banks, discharging over 20,000 cubic feet per second and proving the area’s flood risk.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
